    <string name="about_review_prompt">Is this app helpful? Your review helps us keep growing.</string>
    <string name="about_footer">Developed by ChifuzApps</string>
    <string name="about_content">
    EnfermerApp was born from a real need: reliable calculation tools that won\'t fail you in the middle of a shift. This project is the result of a collaboration between software developers and active nursing professionals.\n\n
    Priority in Emergencies\n
    We know every second counts. That\'s why the app is optimized to give you the results you need instantly. No full-screen ads will be shown until after you have viewed your calculation result, ensuring the speed your work demands.\n\n
    Focus Mode\n
    For those high-demand moments where you need zero distractions, we designed \"Focus Mode.\" By watching a single short video, you can clear the app of full-screen ads for 4 hours, allowing you to focus all your attention on patient care.\n\n
    Privacy and Support\n
    Your privacy comes first: we do not collect personal data. If you have any suggestions or find something to improve, please email us at contact@chifuzapps.com.\n\n
    Thank you for choosing us to support you in your daily clinical practice.
</string>

    <string name="help_dosis_title">Dosage Calculation Guide</string>
    <string name="help_btn_ok">UNDERSTOOD</string>

    <string name="help_std_intro">This calculation uses the simple rule of three to obtain the exact volume (ml) to be drawn from a medication based on medical orders.</string>
    <string name="help_std_terms_header">Glossary of Terms</string>
    <string name="help_std_term_dosis">• <b>Dose to administer:</b> The amount prescribed by the doctor for the patient.</string>
    <string name="help_std_term_volumen">• <b>Medication volume:</b> The total liquid contained in the ampoule or vial (Solvent).</string>
    <string name="help_std_term_concentracion">• <b>Total concentration:</b> The total mg or units present in that volume (Solute).</string>

    <string name="help_std_formula_header">Applied Formula (Rule of 3)</string>
    <string name="help_std_formula_body">\"Result (ml) = (Desired dose × Ampoule volume) / Total concentration\"</string>

    <string name="help_weight_intro">Used when the dose is calculated based on the patient\'s body mass, ensuring personalized dosing.</string>
    <string name="help_weight_term_dosis">• <b>Dose per Kg:</b> Amount of drug indicated for each kilo of weight (e.g., 5mg/kg).</string>
    <string name="help_weight_term_peso">• <b>Patient weight:</b> Current weight in kilograms.</string>
    <string name="help_weight_term_max">• <b>Maximum Dose (Optional):</b> Safety limit. The app will notify you if the calculation exceeds this value.</string>

    <string name="help_weight_formula_header">Applied Formula</string>
    <string name="help_weight_formula_body">\"Total Dose = Dose per Kg × Patient Weight\"</string>


    <string name="help_perfusion_title">Infusion Calculation Guide</string>

    <string name="help_perfusion_intro">This module allows you to calculate the infusion rate of parenteral solutions based on the total volume and the prescribed time.</string>

    <string name="help_perfusion_factors_header">Equivalencies (Drop Factor)</string>
    <string name="help_perfusion_factor_macro">• <b>Macrodrip:</b> Assumes a ratio of 20 drops per 1 ml.</string>
    <string name="help_perfusion_factor_micro">• <b>Microdrip:</b> Assumes a ratio of 60 microdrops per 1 ml.</string>

    <string name="help_perfusion_results_header">Interpreting Results</string>
    <string name="help_perfusion_res_gtts">• <b>Drops/min:</b> The physical drip rate you must set in the delivery system.</string>
    <string name="help_perfusion_res_mlhr">• <b>Rate (ml/h):</b> Volumetric flow per hour, frequently used in infusion pumps.</string>
    <string name="help_perfusion_res_mlmin">• <b>Flow (ml/min):</b> Amount of solution administered to the patient per minute.</string>

    <string name="help_perfusion_formula_header">Applied Formula</string>
    <string name="help_perfusion_formula_body">\"Drops/min = (Volume × Factor) / Time (min)\"</string>

    <string name="help_perfusion_sync_header">Rhythm Synchronization</string>
    <string name="help_perfusion_sync_body">The \"Sync\" option opens a visual and audible metronome adjusted to the calculated result, allowing you to calibrate manual dripping with total precision.</string>


    <string name="help_sync_title">Rhythm Synchronization</string>
    <string name="help_sync_intro">This tool allows you to validate or calibrate manual dripping in two different ways.</string>

    <string name="help_sync_manual_header">Manual Mode (Tapping)</string>
    <string name="help_sync_manual_body">Tap the central blue button **each time you see a drop fall** in the drip chamber. The app will average the time between taps to show you the current actual rate (GTT/MIN).</string>

    <string name="help_sync_metro_header">Metronome Mode</string>
    <string name="help_sync_metro_body">Generates a constant visual and audible signal. Adjust the IV flow control clamp until the drops fall **at exactly the same time** as the metronome pulse.</string>

    <string name="help_sync_tip_header">Precision Tip</string>
    <string name="help_sync_tip_body">For a more stable result in manual mode, it is recommended to perform at least 5 or 6 consecutive taps.</string>


    <string name="help_edad_title">Infant Age Guide</string>
    <string name="help_edad_intro">Corrected age calculation is essential for evaluating the growth and neurocognitive development of preterm infants.</string>
    <string name="help_edad_cron_header">Chronological Age</string>
    <string name="help_edad_cron_body">The time elapsed since the actual moment of birth. It is calculated by subtracting the birth date from the current date.</string>
    <string name="help_edad_corr_header">Corrected Age</string>
    <string name="help_edad_corr_body">The age the child would be if born on the expected due date. It is used to adjust expectations for physical and motor development.</string>
    <string name="help_edad_prema_header">Preterm Calculation</string>
    <string name="help_edad_prema_body">To correct the age, the missing weeks of gestation are subtracted from the chronological age.\n\n<b>Important:</b> If the baby has not yet reached the expected due date, the result will indicate the time remaining to reach that milestone.</string>
    <string name="help_edad_tip_header">Application Reference</string>
    <string name="help_edad_tip_body">Pediatric follow-up protocols typically apply corrected age adjustment until 2 years of age.</string>

